# Ported from samples/GCP/ProcessEngineering: Create_Doc_Agent
# (process_agents/common/doc_creation_agent.py), a standalone 2-stage
# action -- regenerate the flow/architecture diagram, then the final Word
# document -- from whatever process or design JSON is ALREADY saved on
# disk. NO re-analysis, NO design regeneration, NO compliance/simulation
# review, and the saved JSON itself is never modified. This is
# deliberately NOT process.hocon's Process_Pipeline / design.hocon's
# Design_Doc_Pipeline run with its early steps skipped -- those networks
# have no entry point that starts midway through, and forcing a "just
# regenerate" request through either of them would re-run the full
# generate/review cycle, exactly what this network exists to avoid.
#
# Domain-agnostic by design, matching the ADK original's own single
# Create_Doc_Agent (its own router sends BOTH "regenerate the process
# document" and "regenerate the design document" here). When the user's
# own request names which one they mean, Regenerate_Document_Agent passes
# that through explicitly as schema_type -- only a genuinely generic
# "regenerate the document" falls back to auto-detecting from whichever
# JSON file is actually on disk (generate_clean_diagram/
# create_standard_doc_from_file's own detect_schema_type_from_disk),
# which is correct only when at most one of the two files exists: it
# always resolves to "process" whenever both do, confirmed directly to
# silently regenerate the wrong document otherwise.
{
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",

    "metadata": {
        "description": "Regenerates the current process or design document's flow diagram and final Word document from whatever is already saved on disk -- no re-analysis, no compliance/simulation review, just re-rendering the existing content.",
        "tags": ["process", "design", "process-engineering-port"],
        "sample_queries": [
            "Please regenerate the process document.",
            "Regenerate the design document."
        ]
    },

    "tools": [
        {
            "name": "Regenerate_Document_Agent",

            "function": {
                "description": """
I regenerate ONLY the flow/architecture diagram and the final Word document for the current process
or design -- from whatever is already saved on disk. I never re-run analysis, design generation, or
compliance/simulation review, and I never change the saved process/design content itself. Tell me to
regenerate the document.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {"type": "string", "description": "The user's regenerate-document request."}
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },

            "instructions": """
# ROLE
You regenerate ONLY the flow/architecture diagram and the final Word document from whatever process
or design JSON is already saved on disk. You NEVER re-run analysis, design generation, compliance
review, or simulation, and you NEVER modify the saved JSON itself -- that is every other network's
job, on a separate request.

# DETERMINE schema_type FIRST
Before calling either tool, check whether "inquiry" itself names a domain:
- If it explicitly says "process" / "process document" / "the process", schema_type = "process".
- If it explicitly says "design" / "design document" / "HLD" / "LLD" / "architecture document" /
  "the design", schema_type = "design".
- Otherwise (a generic "regenerate the document" with no domain named), leave schema_type unset --
  do NOT guess. This case falls back to whichever single file actually exists on disk; if BOTH a
  process and a design document exist and the request is this generic, that is a genuinely
  ambiguous request -- regenerate whichever the most recent turns in this conversation were about,
  or if that's unclear too, ask the user to say "the process document" or "the design document".

# SEQUENCE
1. Call regenerate_flow_diagram, passing {"schema_type": ...} if you determined one above (omit the
   argument entirely otherwise). ALWAYS produces some diagram, even a minimal placeholder when
   nothing real is saved yet for that domain -- so its own result alone does NOT tell you whether a
   real document exists to regenerate. Always proceed to step 2 regardless of what this returns.
2. Call regenerate_document with the SAME schema_type determination (no "process_name" argument
   needed -- the saved JSON's own name/title takes precedence over the fallback). This is the real
   check: if its result starts with "ERROR", there is no actual saved document of that type yet --
   reply that there is nothing to regenerate, and that they should create one first (e.g. "create a
   process for ..." / "create a design document for ..."). If it starts with "SUCCESS", report that
   the flow diagram and Word document were both regenerated from the current saved content.

Plain prose only in your final reply -- no raw JSON, tool names, or internal field names.
""",
            "tools": ["regenerate_flow_diagram", "regenerate_document"]
        },

        {
            "name": "regenerate_flow_diagram",
            "function": {
                "description": "Regenerates the flow/architecture diagram from whichever process/design JSON is already saved on disk.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "schema_type": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "enum": ["process", "design"],
                            "description": "Pass this when the user's own request names which document they mean. Omit it only for a genuinely generic request -- it then auto-detects from whichever single file exists on disk, which is ambiguous whenever both do."
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "class": "edge_inference_tool.RegenerateFlowDiagramCodedTool"
        },
        {
            "name": "regenerate_document",
            "function": {
                "description": "Regenerates the final Word document from whichever process/design JSON is already saved on disk.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "schema_type": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "enum": ["process", "design"],
                            "description": "Pass this when the user's own request names which document they mean. Omit it only for a genuinely generic request -- it then auto-detects from whichever single file exists on disk, which is ambiguous whenever both do."
                        },
                        "process_name": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional fallback document title, used only if the saved JSON itself has no name/title."
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "class": "doc_generation_tool.RegenerateDocumentCodedTool"
        }
    ]
}
